<!-- SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY               -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h1>Section 1: Executive Summary</h1>

<p>
    <b>CivicLens</b> transforms a basic Java Swing complaint management application into a production-grade, explainable, privacy-aware, and accountable civic complaint resolution platform. Traditional civic helpdesks and complaint management prototypes are crippled by black-box prioritizations, unmonitored ticket queues, duplicate noise during infrastructure disasters, arbitrary status overrides without accountability, and opaque or fabricated analytics.
</p>

<p>
    CivicLens addresses these systemic failures by introducing <b>five interconnected engineering capabilities</b>: explainable multi-dimensional triage, deterministic duplicate detection, configurable SLA policy enforcement, validated lifecycle state transitions with authenticated citizen appeals, and outcome-focused analytics. Every single capability produces traceable, tamper-evident database records and binds directly into the end-to-end complaint lifecycle.
</p>

<!-- Metric Cards Grid -->
<table style="width:100%; border:none; margin:14pt 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="width:20%; border:none; padding:4pt;">
            <div class="metric-box">
